{"page":770,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.42424,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"756 Chapter 13: Vector-Valued Functions and Motion in Space"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.10835,"w":0.52837,"h":0.04734,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Differentiation Rules for Vector Functions Let u and v be differentiable vector functions of t, C a constant vector, c any sca- lar, and ƒ any differentiable scalar function."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.16255,"w":0.27769,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"1. Constant Function Rule: d dtC = 0"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.18937,"w":0.34632,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"2. Scalar Multiple Rules: d dt 3cu(t)4 = cu′(t)"},{"x":0.57206,"y":0.21943,"w":0.23838,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d dt 3ƒ(t)u(t)4 = ƒ′(t)u(t) + ƒ(t)u′(t)"},{"x":0.35361,"y":0.24948,"w":0.43312,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"3. Sum Rule: d dt 3u(t) + v(t)4 = u′(t) + v′(t)"},{"x":0.35361,"y":0.27954,"w":0.43312,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"4. Difference Rule: d dt 3u(t) - v(t)4 = u′(t) - v′(t)"},{"x":0.35361,"y":0.30959,"w":0.48951,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01918,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"5. Dot Product Rule: d dt 3u(t) # v(t)4 = u′(t) # v(t) + u(t) # v′(t)"},{"x":0.0583,"y":0.32265,"w":0.23146,"h":0.06777,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"When you use the Cross Product Rule, remember to preserve the order of the factors. If u comes first on the left side of the equation, it must also come first on the right or the signs will be wrong."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.33965,"w":0.52992,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"6. Cross Product Rule: d dt 3u(t) * v(t)4 = u′(t) * v(t) + u(t) * v′(t)"},{"x":0.35362,"y":0.3697,"w":0.39895,"h":0.0305,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"7. Chain Rule: d dt 3u(ƒ(t))4 = ƒ′(t)u′(ƒ(t))"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.44361,"w":0.59307,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We will prove the product rules and Chain Rule but leave the rules for constants, scalar multiples, sums, and differences as exercises."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.4847,"w":